  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Load a shoulder-motion trial and compare, frame by frame, how different Euler/swing-twist decompositions break humerus and scapula orientation into sub-rotations, using linked animated 3D bone views and time-series angle plots. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
